    "bootstrap": "2,000-replicate initialization-level bootstrap (resampling complete per-init gradient vectors with replacement within each cell, recomputing the per-parameter variance statistic per replicate, then refitting the full log10(variance) ~ grid-axis regression) for every headline and fixed-depth/fixed-qubit regression.",
    "nonpositive_variance_handling": "Before any log10 transform, a variance estimate <= 0 (possible for a bootstrap replicate that happens to resample near-duplicate initializations, though not observed in the point-estimate data) is floored at 1e-300 (far below any physically meaningful gradient variance in this experiment) rather than dropped, so every bootstrap replicate still contributes a finite slope estimate; floored replicates are counted and reported separately."
  }
